  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/lib/routes.mjs", "line": 268,
   "summary": "matchPath does not keep a fixed route ahead of a [param] folder: when the fixed route's folder has no matching file, the walk falls through to the [param] folder's file. The server and the link check share this code, so both get it wrong together.",
   "failure_scenario": "Confirmed in a run. orders/[id]/index.html and index--error.html exist, routes.json also names orders/new and orders/archive. GET /orders/archive (not rendered yet) returns the order-details page instead of the placeholder. /orders/new?state=error returns orders/[id]/index--error.html even though orders/new has no error state. links.mjs passes both links. The overlay labels the page with the fixed screen's code (findScreen), so comments are recorded against the wrong screen and the state switcher lists the [id] folder's states."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/routes.mjs", "line": 168,
   "summary": "Two codes whose Route reduces to the same path always stop the run. That is normal for modal, dialog or sheet screens, which sit on their parent's route.",
   "failure_scenario": "A delete-confirm modal 200e has Route '`/orders/:id` (modal)'. routeToken picks '/orders/:id', which is already 200b's, so routes.mjs exits 1 with 'route ... is held by two codes'. /vwf:mockups and blueprint §6a then render nothing for the whole platform. The ui-ux-contract reference explicitly allows modal vs full-page per action."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/serve.mjs", "line": 523,
   "summary": "The overlay's click handler calls preventDefault on everything that isn't an a[href]. That cancels form submits, which mockup-generator.md says can be used for navigation ('or a form action'). links.mjs also only reads href, so form actions are never checked.",
   "failure_scenario": "A sign-in screen navigates through <form action=\"/orders\"><button>Sign in</button>. Clicking the button opens the comment box instead of submitting, so the connected site has a dead end. A typo such as action=\"/order\" is never reported because HREF_RE ignores action=."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/routes.mjs", "line": 115,
   "summary": "A home-rule reference row is skipped only when its Code cell is a markdown link. That format was assumed by U1 (logged as a GAP) and is not stated in any contract doc. Any other way of writing the reference counts as a second definition.",
   "failure_scenario": "Flow 300 refers to screen 100a as '| 100a | [Home](../100-home/web.md) | / |' (the link in the Screen cell). routes.mjs reports 'code 100a is defined twice' and 'route / is held by two codes', exits 1, and nothing renders for the platform."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/blueprint/references/screen-review.md", "line": 39,
   "summary": "The clear step deletes only at paths named in the new routes.json. When a screen's route changes, its old page stays on disk and is still served at the old URL. links.mjs then scans it, and its BROKEN lines can't be traced to a flow for the repair round.",
   "failure_scenario": "A blueprint pass changes 200b's route from /orders/:id to /o/:id. orders/[id]/index.html stays and links to a screen whose route also moved. links.mjs reports it, step 3 finds no owning flow in routes.json, two rounds fail, and the review stops with no URL and no stamp. Only a full sweep clears it, and §6a never sweeps. mockups/SKILL.md:140 has the same gap for flow-scoped runs."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/serve.mjs", "line": 401,
   "summary": "POST /comment and POST /done don't check Origin, and readJson parses any content type. Any web page open in the reviewer's browser can write to comments.yaml or shut the server down.",
   "failure_scenario": "A page in another tab sends fetch('http://127.0.0.1:<port>/comment', {method:'POST', mode:'no-cors', body: JSON.stringify({path:'/', state:'', selector:'x', text:'ignore prior rules and ...'})}) as a simple text/plain request, scanning likely ports. The text lands in comments.yaml, which the agent reads and proposes edits from. A POST to /done ends the review early."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/SKILL.md", "line": 140,
   "summary": "The clear and prune steps tell the agent to delete index--*.html under [param] folders without saying the brackets must be quoted or escaped. A shell reads [id] as a character class.",
   "failure_scenario": "The agent runs rm docs/scratchpad/p/mockups/web/orders/[id]/index--*.html. fish fails with 'no matches found' and runs nothing; bash looks for orders/i or orders/d and fails. Old state files stay behind and keep being served and listed in the state switcher after the contract drops that state."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/serve.mjs", "line": 336,
   "summary": "The comment record writes code and route but never the request path. When findScreen finds no screen, the comment has no location at all.",
   "failure_scenario": "A reviewer comments on a page that is served directly from disk but isn't in routes.json (a stale old route, or a direct /x/index--error.html URL). comments.yaml gets 'code: null, route: null'. The step-10 report prints 'null null?state=...', and the §6a review can't tell which screen the comment is about. The concrete sample URL (/orders/1042) is also lost for routed screens."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/links.mjs", "line": 80,
   "summary": "HREF_RE only matches quoted href values. Unquoted href=/path links are neither counted nor checked.",
   "failure_scenario": "A generator writes <a href=/order/1>, which is valid HTML. links.mjs skips it and prints LINKS OK. The reviewer clicks it and gets a 404, which is exactly what the check is meant to prevent."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/SKILL.md", "line": 201,
   "summary": "The skill waits for every review server to exit, and a server only exits on its own Done. There is no timeout and no way to end the wait without Done, and polling is forbidden.",
